;; Written by Claude, 2026-11-19, for bug 31 (PLAN.md, "Ongoing bug
;; fixing"); reviewed by the user, 2026-11-19. Why this is right:
;; - A structured constant indexed with a variable is selected from its
;;   storage in POC_CONST, L_CONST_<n> (section 16, proposal 7), as a
;;   variable of its type in POC_DATA would be (Locate): an element in
;;   index mode, L_CONST_1[R0] (SumSquares), L_CONST_5[R0] (Digit); a
;;   row of a two-dimensional table by its size, MULL2 #8 and MOVAB,
;;   then its element (R0)[R1] (GridAt, both ways of writing it); an
;;   element of a field at the field's offset, L_CONST_4+4[R0]
;;   (NamedValue); a field of an element (PointX); an element copied
;;   whole, MOVC3 (PointAt); a row's address and length passed to an
;;   open array (RowSum).
;; - Each index is checked as a variable's is, trap 2 at its line and
;;   column; the constants' data is as in vax-structured-constants.
; ConstTables, written by poc (doc/developer/vax-macro32-backend.md)
